    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308-a7">

                <pb facs="0419" n="311" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg311"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7 in No. 910.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr.
                            Kustel.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Royalist</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">at
                            Butaritari</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-07"><hi rendition="#italic">July 7,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">memorandum.</hi></p>
                <p>You having this day declined to make suitable reparation to Tabantia, the Tarawa
                    native, whom, by your own admission, you assaulted on Tarawa Island, about
                    November, 1891, I shall request the commander in chief to communicate with the
                    United States Government on the subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ed. H. M. Davis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain and one of Her Majesty’s Deputy
                            Commissioners for the Western Pacific.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
